    "result_text": "No dangling references. The build compiles clean and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked everything that keys off the household to use it.\n\n**Household identity (`HouseholdKey`)** \u2014 now the canonical equivalence over `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`, producing `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`. It remains the single place that decides household equivalence, so duplicate detection, size counting, and id assignment stay in agreement.\n\n**`HouseholdIdGenerator`** \u2014 now returns the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over that key (`normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`), dropping the old `HH-`/uppercase formatting to match the spec exactly. Owners with the same last name and postcode get the same id automatically.\n\n**`DuplicateOwnerValidator`** \u2014 now rejects (409) when an existing owner belongs to the same household (same key), rather than only on an exact `identityKey` match. This is what makes a second owner sharing last name + postcode a household duplicate.\n\n**`HouseholdRegistrar` \u2192 `HouseholdSizeCalculator`** \u2014 renamed and narrowed to a single responsibility. Since the id is deterministic and every owner already carries it, there's no linking/back-filling to do; it just counts the joining owner plus existing housemates via the shared `HouseholdKey`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 now:\n- always computes and stamps the deterministic `householdId` (from last name + postcode);\n- treats `sharesHousehold` purely as a *bypass* of the duplicate block;\n- when declared, marks the owner as **not** a possible duplicate (a declared member isn't a suspected duplicate); otherwise runs the duplicate check and possible-duplicate detection;\n- always computes `householdSize` from the computed household.\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions/examples for `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` to reflect the new postcode-based, always-present keying.\n\nOne consequence worth flagging: because any non-declared second owner sharing last name + postcode is now rejected with 409 before reaching possible-duplicate detection, the `possibleDuplicate` flag is effectively never set to true anymore (declared members are explicitly not flagged, and non-declared collisions are blocked). That follows directly from the spec \u2014 the household collision that used to be a \"soft\" flag is now a hard 409 \u2014 but I left the detector in place since it remains the correct, honest implementation of that check.",
